---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import heroImg from "../../assets/LandingImage.jpg";
import BlogImg from "../../assets/blogImages/Blog34.webp";

const breadcrumbs = [
    { label: "Home", href: "/" },
    { label: "Blogs", href: "/blogs" },
    { label: "Plan Perfect Chinese Food Party", href: "#", current: true }
];

const blogData = {
    title: "How to Plan the Perfect Chinese Food Party at Home",
    metaTitle: "How to Plan the Perfect Chinese Food Party at Home",
    metaDescription:
        "Hosting a Chinese food party at home? Get expert tips on menu planning, ordering the best starters & mains from Vanchu Hut in Ghaziabad.",
    image: BlogImg,
    publishDate: "2026-04-21",
    introduction:
        "Planning a party at home but tired of the same old pizza and sandwiches? Why not spice things up with a Chinese food party? Whether it's a birthday, game night, or just a casual get-together with family and friends, Chinese cuisine offers something for everyone, from crispy starters to saucy mains and comforting noodles. At Vanchu Hut, located in Pratap Vihar, Ghaziabad, we've helped hundreds of customers host unforgettable Chinese food parties at home. Here's your step-by-step guide to making it perfect, stress-free, and delicious.",
    steps: [
        {
            title: "Step 1: Choose Your Chinese Party Menu Wisely",
            content:
                "The key to a great Chinese food party is variety without overcomplicating. Stick to 3-4 starters, 2-3 mains, and 1-2 carb options like noodles or rice, plus a dessert or drink. Start with crowd-favorite appetizers like Crispy Chili Potatoes, Veg Manchurian, and Steamed Dumplings. For mains, opt for Mixed Vegetable Hakka Noodles and Veg Fried Rice paired with Manchurian Gravy or Chili Paneer. This combination ensures both dry and saucy dishes, satisfying different palates."
        },
        {
            title: "Step 2: Decide Between Homemade, Takeout, or a Mix",
            content:
                "Let's be real: cooking an entire Chinese spread from scratch can be exhausting. At Vanchu Hut, we recommend a smart hybrid approach. Prepare one or two simple dishes at home, like a fresh salad or steamed rice, and order the rest from us. Our takeout and delivery service ensures your party food arrives hot, fresh, and perfectly packed. You get restaurant-quality flavors like our Special Veg Noodles and Honey Chili Potatoes without spending hours in the kitchen. Plus, you'll have more time to enjoy your guests."
        },
        {
            title: "Step 3: Portion Planning for a Crowd",
            content:
                "A common party mistake is either running out of food or wasting leftovers. As a rule of thumb for Chinese food, order 1 starter per 2-3 people, 1 main dish (noodles or rice) per 2-3 people, and 1 gravy dish per 3-4 people. For example, for 6 adults, order 2-3 starters, 2 noodle or rice dishes, and 1-2 gravy mains. At Vanchu Hut, our portion sizes are generous, so you can always rely on our staff to guide you. Mention the number of guests while ordering, and we'll recommend the perfect quantity."
        },
        {
            title: "Step 4: Setup and Serving Tips for Chinese Theme",
            content:
                "Presentation matters. Use small bowls for dipping sauces like chili sauce, soy sauce, and vinegar, and place chopsticks next to plates for authenticity. If you want to go the extra mile, use red and gold decorations, lucky colors in Chinese culture. Keep extra napkins and wet wipes handy because Chinese food can be delightfully messy. And don't forget drinks. Lemon iced tea, jasmine tea, or a simple chilled beer pair wonderfully with spicy Indo-Chinese dishes."
        },
        {
            title: "Step 5: Don't Forget the Starters, The Real Party Heroes",
            content:
                "We've said it before, and we'll say it again: starters make or break a Chinese food party. Check out our detailed guide on Best Starters to Order at a Chinese Restaurant for deeper insights. But here's a quick cheat sheet: for a party of 8, order a platter of Crispy Chili Potatoes, a large Veg Manchurian (dry), and two types of dumplings (steamed and fried). These will keep guests happy while the mains are being served. Pro tip: ask for extra schezwan sauce on the side, it disappears fast."
        }
    ],
    faqs: [
        {
            question: "How much Chinese food should I order per person?",
            answer:
                "Generally, 200-250g of noodles or rice and 3-4 pieces of starters per person is enough. At Vanchu Hut, we suggest ordering for 1.5x the number of guests if you want leftovers."
        },
        {
            question: "Can I order a mix of Jain and regular Chinese food?",
            answer:
                "Yes. Vanchu Hut prepares Jain-friendly Chinese dishes (no onion, no garlic) on request. Just inform us while placing the order."
        },
        {
            question: "What are the best Chinese dishes for a kids' party?",
            answer:
                "Kids love Honey Chili Potatoes, Spring Rolls, and plain Veg Noodles. Avoid extra spicy Manchurian for young taste buds."
        },
        {
            question: "How far in advance should I order for a party?",
            answer:
                "At least 2-3 hours in advance for standard orders. For large parties (15+ people), call us a day ahead so we can allocate extra preparation time."
        },
        {
            question: "Does Vanchu Hut provide disposable plates and cutlery?",
            answer:
                "Yes, on request we can include eco-friendly plates, napkins, and forks or chopsticks with your party order."
        }
    ],
    conclusion:
        "Planning a Chinese food party at home doesn't have to be complicated. With the right menu, smart ordering from Vanchu Hut, and a little bit of setup, you'll be the host everyone talks about. We take pride in being one of the best restaurants in Ghaziabad for Chinese cuisine, and we'd love to be a part of your celebration. Visit us or order online today and let's make your party deliciously memorable!",
    contact: {
        name: "Vanchu Hut",
        address: "Santosh Medical Intersection, Block H Pratap Vihar, Ghaziabad, UP 201009",
        phone: "+91 9971135534",
        hours: "Mon-Fri 11AM-10PM, Sat-Sun 12PM-11PM"
    }
};
---

<Layout title={blogData.metaTitle} description={blogData.metaDescription}>
    <section class="font-agdasima">
        <Image
            src={heroImg}
            class="scale-100 w-screen h-[168px] transform -translate-y-[100px] md:-translate-y-[60px] object-cover"
            alt="Header Image, shows picture of Various Chinese Food on a Table"
        />
    </section>

    <nav class="flex px-4" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <ol class="flex items-center space-x-2">
            {breadcrumbs.map((item, index) => (
                <li class="flex items-center">
                    {index > 0 && (
                        <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-gray-400 mx-2" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20">
                            <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M7.293 14.707a1 1 0 010-1.414L10.586 10 7.293 6.707a1 1 0 011.414-1.414l4 4a1 1 0 010 1.414l-4 4a1 1 0 01-1.414 0z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
                        </svg>
                    )}
                    {item.current ? (
                        <span class="text-gray-600" aria-current="page">{item.label}</span>
                    ) : (
                        <a href={item.href} class="text-primary hover:text-primary/80">{item.label}</a>
                    )}
                </li>
            ))}
        </ol>
    </nav>

    <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-8">
        <div class="relative h-[400px] mb-8 rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
            <Image
                format="avif"
                src={blogData.image}
                alt="How to plan the perfect Chinese food party at home"
                class="w-full h-full object-cover"
            />
        </div>

        <article class="prose prose-lg max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-8">
            <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-primary mb-8">{blogData.title}</h1>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded-lg mb-8">
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Table of Contents</h2>
                <ol class="list-decimal pl-4 space-y-1">
                    {blogData.steps.map((step) => (
                        <li>{step.title}</li>
                    ))}
                    <li>FAQs</li>
                    <li>Conclusion</li>
                </ol>
            </div>

            <p class="text-gray-700 mb-8">{blogData.introduction}</p>

            {blogData.steps.map((step) => (
                <section class="mb-12">
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-secondary mb-4">{step.title}</h2>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">{step.content}</p>
                </section>
            ))}

            <section class="bg-primary/10 p-6 rounded-lg mb-12">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">FAQs</h2>
                <div class="space-y-5">
                    {blogData.faqs.map((faq, index) => (
                        <div>
                            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Q{index + 1}: {faq.question}</h3>
                            <p class="text-gray-700">A: {faq.answer}</p>
                        </div>
                    ))}
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-12">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-secondary mb-4">Conclusion</h2>
                <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">{blogData.conclusion}</p>

                <div class="bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg">
                    <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">{blogData.contact.name}</h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 mb-2"><strong>Address:</strong> {blogData.contact.address}</p>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 mb-2"><strong>Phone:</strong> {blogData.contact.phone}</p>
                    <p class="text-gray-700"><strong>Hours:</strong> {blogData.contact.hours}</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <div class="flex justify-center gap-6 mt-12">
                <a href="/menu" class="bg-secondary text-white px-8 py-3 rounded-full hover:bg-secondary/90">
                    View Our Menu
                </a>
                <a href="/contact" class="bg-primary text-white px-8 py-3 rounded-full hover:bg-primary/90">
                    Contact Us
                </a>
            </div>
        </article>
    </main>
</Layout>
